NNAAMMEE
       sldtoppm - convert an AutoCAD slide file to a PPM image


SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ssllddttooppppmm  [--aaddjjuusstt]  [--ddiirr]  [{--hheeiigghhtt|--yyssiizzee}  _s] [--iinnffoo] [{--lliibb|--LLiibb}
       _n_a_m_e] [--ssccaallee _s] [--vveerrbboossee] [{--wwiiddtthh|--xxssiizzee} _s] [_s_l_i_d_e_f_i_l_e]

       All options can be abbreviated to their shortest unique prefix.


DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ssllddttooppppmm reads an AutoCAD® slide file and outputs a PPM image.  If  you
       don't  specify  _s_l_i_d_e_f_i_l_e,  ssllddttooppppmm  reads  input from Standard Input.
       ssllddttooppppmm uses the ppppmmddrraaww library to convert the vector and polygon in‐
       formation in the slide file to a raster; see the file ppppmmddrraaww..hh for de‐
       tails on this package.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), ssllddttooppppmm recognizes the
       following command line options:



       --aaddjjuusstt
              If the display on which the slide  file  was  created  had  non-
              square  pixels,  when  you  process  the slide with ssllddttooppppmm and
              don't specify --aaddjjuusstt, ssllddttooppppmm issues the following warning;

              Warning - pixels on source screen were non-square.

       Specifying --aaddjjuusstt will correct the image width to compensate.   Speci‐
       fying  the --aaddjjuusstt option causes ssllddttooppppmm to scale the width of the im‐
       age so that pixels in the resulting PPM image  are  square  (and  hence
       circles  appear  as  true  circles, not ellipses).  The scaling is per‐
       formed in the vector domain, before scan converting the  objects.   The
       results  are,  therefore,  superior  in appearance to what you'd obtain
       were you to perform the equivalent scaling with ppaammssccaallee after the bit‐
       map had been created.


       --ddiirr   The input is assumed to be an AutoCAD slide library file.  A di‐
              rectory listing each slide in the library is printed on standard
              error.


       --hheeiigghhtt _s_i_z_e
              Scales  the  image  in the vector domain so it is _s_i_z_e pixels in
              height.  If you don't specify --wwiiddtthh or --xxssiizzee, ssllddttooppppmm adjusts
              the width to preserve the pixel aspect ratio.


       --iinnffoo  Dump  the  slide  file  header on standard error, displaying the
              original screen size and aspect ratio among other information.


       --lliibb _n_a_m_e
              Extracts the slide with the given _n_a_m_e from  the  slide  library
              given  as  input.  ssllddttooppppmm converts the specified _n_a_m_e to upper
              case.


       --LLiibb _n_a_m_e
              Extracts the slide with the given _n_a_m_e from  the  slide  library
              given  as  input.   ssllddttooppppmm uses _n_a_m_e in the case specified; it
              does not convert it to upper case.


       --ssccaallee _s
              Scales the image by factor _s, which may be  any  floating  point
              value greater than zero.  ssllddttooppppmm does the scaling after aspect
              ratio adjustment, if any.  Since it does the scaling in the vec‐
              tor  domain,  before rasterisation, the results look much better
              than running the output of ssllddttooppppmm through ppaammssccaallee.


       --vveerrbboossee
              Dumps the slide file header and lists every vector  and  polygon
              to Standard Error.


       --wwiiddtthh _s_i_z_e
              Scales the image in the vector domain so it is _s_i_z_e pixels wide.
              If you don't specify --hheeiigghhtt or  --yyssiizzee,  ssllddttooppppmm  adjusts  the
              height to preserve the pixel aspect ratio.


       --xxssiizzee _s_i_z_e
              Scales the image in the vector domain so it is _s_i_z_e pixels wide.
              If you don't specify --hheeiigghhtt or  --yyssiizzee,  ssllddttooppppmm  adjusts  the
              height to preserve the pixel aspect ratio.


       --yyssiizzee _s_i_z_e
              Scales  the  image  in the vector domain so it is _s_i_z_e pixels in
              height.  If you don't specify --wwiiddtthh or --xxssiizzee, ssllddttooppppmm adjusts
              the width to preserve the pixel aspect ratio.




LLIIMMIITTAATTIIOONNSS
       ssllddttooppppmm  can convert only Level 2 slides.  Level 1 format has been ob‐
       solete since the advent of AutoCAD Release 9 in 1987, and was not  por‐
       table across machine architectures.

       Slide library items with names containing 8 bit (such as ISO) or 16 bit
       (Kanji, for example) characters may not be found when chosen  with  the
       --lliibb  option  unless  ssllddttooppppmm  was built with character set conversion
       functions appropriate to the locale.  You can  always  retrieve  slides
       from libraries regardless of the character set by using the --LLiibb option
       and specifying the precise name of library member.  Use the --ddiirr option
       to list the slides in a library if you're unsure of the exact name.


